5.1 Introduction
Motion planning is a longstanding problem of interest in robotics, with previous approaches ranging from potential fields [139, 213, 275], sampling [24, 83, 134, 136, 150, 158, 244], search [98, 145, 163] and trajectory optimization [66, 218, 229, 246]. Despite being ubiquitous, these methods are often slow at producing solutions since they largely plan from scratch at test time, re-using little to no information outside of the current problem and what is engineered by a human designer. Since motion-planning is a core component of the
