ieving 81% performance vs. 31% and 44%. We visualize an example trajectory in Fig. 5.4. Our method performs well on in-distribution objects such as the book and board game, but struggles on out of distribution objects such as the toy sword, which is double the size of objects at training time. We additionally deploy our method on significantly out of
57


